# Astro Component Patterns

When creating or editing `.astro` files in `src/`, follow these patterns exactly.

## Skeleton

```astro
---
// ── Typed data / constants ──
interface Item {
  name: string;
  url: string;
}

const items: Item[] = [
  { name: "Example", url: "#" },
];
---

<section class="my-section" id="my-section">
  <div class="container">
    {
      items.map((item) => (
        <a href={item.url} class="card">{item.name}</a>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
  .my-section { /* ... */ }
</style>

<script>
  // vanilla, type-annotated
  const el = document.getElementById("my-section");
  if (el) { /* ... */ }
</script>
```

## Rules

- **Frontmatter first**, always fenced with `---`.
- Define repeated/mutable data as a typed array of objects in the frontmatter — never duplicate markup by hand.
- Use `set:html={svgString}` for inline SVG icons kept in data objects.
- Conditional rendering uses `{cond && <span/>}`.
- JS variables need null-checks (`if (el)`) since the DOM may not have the node.
- The `<script>` block is bundled/processed by Astro — it runs once on the client. No `type="module"` needed.
- Prefer **scoped** `<style>` (default). Only add `is:global` when the class must apply across components (e.g. `.reveal`, `.container` helpers, section-level styling that the page reuses).
- Keep one `<style>` and one `<script>` per component at the end of the file, in that order.
- Do not add frameworks (`client:load` etc.) unless explicitly requested.

## Naming

- Component files: `PascalCase.astro`.
- CSS classes: `kebab-case`, BEM-ish but not strict (`app-card`, `app-card-header`, `btn-play`).
- IDs for JS hooks: `kebab-case` (`countdown-timer`, `countdown-wrapper`).
